{% comment %}
  The Online Store channel exists only to host Shopify checkout and the
  ParcelPanel order-tracking app proxy on checkout.fastsneakers.com.
  Every page this theme renders is a stale copy of a storefront that now
  lives on Hydrogen at fastsneakers.com, so anyone who lands here --
  returning from the checkout sign-in, clicking the checkout header, or
  following an old backlink -- gets sent to the real storefront instead.

  Never redirects:
    /apps/*        the ParcelPanel proxy must render on this domain
    design mode    so the theme stays editable in the theme editor
    password / challenge / gift card templates, which have no Hydrogen route

  Checkout itself (/checkouts/*, /customer_authentication/*) is not rendered
  by the theme, so nothing here can touch it.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign storefront = 'https://fastsneakers.com'

  assign stay_here = false
  if request.design_mode
    assign stay_here = true
  endif
  if request.path contains '/apps/'
    assign stay_here = true
  endif

  assign protected_templates = 'password,challenge,gift_card,captcha'
  assign template_names = protected_templates | split: ','
  for name in template_names
    if template.name == name
      assign stay_here = true
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Paths Hydrogen mirrors one-for-one, so the visitor keeps their place.
    Anything else (404s, old theme-only routes) goes to the home page.
  endcomment
  assign mirrored = 'index,product,collection,list-collections,page,policy,blog,article,cart,search'
  assign mirrored_names = mirrored | split: ','
  assign keep_path = false
  for name in mirrored_names
    if template.name == name
      assign keep_path = true
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Shop policy pages do not report template.name == 'policy', so the list
    above never matches them and the visitor was dropped on the home page.
    Match on the request path instead. Shopify checkout's footer links to
    these URLs, so losing the path here means a customer in checkout cannot
    read the refund or privacy policy at all.
  endcomment
  if request.path contains '/policies/'
    assign keep_path = true
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  28 Sep 2026 — made crawler-proof for Google Merchant Center.
  Google Shopping links point at THIS domain (the Online Store channel), so
  the redirect must work without JavaScript and must name the exact Hydrogen
  URL, not the home page:
    - `target` is built in Liquid (path preserved on mirrored pages), so the
      meta refresh and the canonical carry the same URL as the JS redirect.
    - The meta refresh is no longer inside <noscript>: a 0-second meta refresh
      is treated by Google as a permanent redirect.
    - The canonical is NOT output here (that made two canonical tags): it is
      rewritten in snippets/meta-tags.liquid to name the Hydrogen page.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign target = storefront
  if keep_path
    assign target = storefront | append: request.path
  endif
-%}
{%- unless stay_here -%}
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ target }}">
  <script>
    (function redirectToStorefront() {
      var STOREFRONT = {{ storefront | json }};
      var KEEP_PATH = {{ keep_path | json }};
      var target = STOREFRONT;
      try {
        if (KEEP_PATH) {
          target += window.location.pathname + window.location.search + window.location.hash;
        }
        window.location.replace(target);
      } catch (error) {
        window.location.href = STOREFRONT;
      }
    })();
  </script>
{%- endunless -%}
